course: dictionary
lesson: 8820
title: Shelter: a safe place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shelter is a word you can use as a noun or a verb. A shelter is a place that keeps you safe. To shelter is to stay somewhere safe, or to keep someone safe. Look at the words around it to see which one is meant.
explain: «Donkey coats are not waterproof like horses' coats, so donkeys need shelter from the rain.» Here shelter is a noun, a place that keeps the rain off. The clue is the rain: the donkeys need somewhere dry to go.
explain: «If you are lost and get wet, you find shelter and put on dry layers.» Find shelter means find a safe place, like a cave, a hut or a tent. Put on dry layers means you change into warm, dry clothes. Both clues show that you are cold and need to be safe.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Does «find a safe place that keeps you dry» make sense? Yes, so shelter is right. Always check your meaning fits the whole sentence.
fact: Shelter can be a noun (a place) or a verb (to stay safe).
fact: «A shelter is a place that keeps you safe from rain, cold, sun or danger.»
fact: «An animal shelter looks after lost or unwanted pets until they get new homes.»
fact: «A shelter is also a place where people without a home can sleep.»
fact: «To shelter» means to stay somewhere safe, or to keep someone safe.
exercise: «Donkey coats are not waterproof, so donkeys need shelter from the rain.» What does shelter mean here? | A loud noise | A cold drink | *A safe place that keeps the rain off | A fast horse
exercise: «If you are lost and get wet, you find shelter and put on dry layers.» Why do you need shelter? | *To stay safe and dry | To find a lost dog | To go for a swim | To make a loud noise
exercise: An animal shelter has 12 dogs. 3 dogs are adopted, and 5 new dogs arrive. How many dogs are in the shelter now? | 17 | 20 | *14 | 9
exercise: «The hikers sheltered under a tree from the storm.» What does sheltered mean here? | Lost their way in the woods | *Stayed somewhere safe from the storm | Walked faster in the rain | Shouted loudly at the storm
exercise: Which sentence uses shelter as a noun, meaning a place? | *«They found a shelter on the mountain.» | «The rain sheltered the hikers.» | «Shelter the lamb from the cold wind.» | «They shelter from the sun under the tree.»
test: «A bus shelter keeps people dry while they wait.» Is shelter a noun or a verb in this sentence? | *Noun, because it is a place | Adverb, because it tells how | Verb, because it is an action | Adjective, because it describes the bus
test: What does an animal shelter do? | *Looks after lost or unwanted pets until they get new homes | Sells pets in shops | Keeps food for the zoo | Builds houses for animals in the woods
exam: Which meaning of shelter fits «The shelter kept the rain off the old bench»? | To sleep in the open | *A place that keeps you safe from the rain | A tall tree in the park | To shout at the rain
